@startuml sequence-payment-flow
!theme plain
autonumber

title Payment Creation Flow - Hyperswitch

actor Customer
participant "Web SDK" as SDK
participant "Router API" as Router
participant "Payment Core" as Core
participant "Routing Engine" as Euclid
participant "Connector\n(e.g., Stripe)" as Connector
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
database "Redis" as Cache
queue "Event Stream" as Events

== Payment Initialization ==

Customer -> SDK: Click "Pay Now"
activate SDK

SDK -> Router: POST /payments\n{amount, currency, merchant_id}
activate Router

Router -> Router: Validate API key
Router -> Cache: GET merchant:config
Cache --> Router: Merchant config

Router -> Core: create_payment(request)
activate Core

Core -> DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
Core -> DB: INSERT payment_intent\nSET status = 'created'
DB --> Core: payment_id

Core -> Cache: SET payment:{id}:lock (NX, EX 30)
Cache --> Core: OK

== Connector Selection ==

Core -> Euclid: evaluate_routing_rules(\nmerchant_id, amount, currency,\npayment_method, customer_location)
activate Euclid

Euclid -> Euclid: Execute WASM rules\n- Check success rates\n- Evaluate cost\n- Apply merchant preferences
Euclid --> Core: Selected connector: "stripe"
deactivate Euclid

Core -> DB: UPDATE payment_intent\nSET connector = 'stripe'

== Payment Processing ==

Core -> Connector: POST /v1/payment_intents\nAuthorization: Bearer sk_xxx\n{amount, currency, payment_method}
activate Connector

Connector -> Connector: Process payment\n- Validate card\n- Check limits\n- Run fraud checks

alt Payment Requires 3DS
    Connector --> Core: 202 Accepted\n{status: requires_action,\nnext_action: {type: redirect_to_url}}
    Core -> DB: UPDATE payment_intent\nSET status = 'requires_customer_action'
    Core --> Router: PaymentResponse\n{requires_action: true, redirect_url}
    Router --> SDK: 202 {redirect_url}
    SDK -> SDK: Open 3DS iframe
    SDK --> Customer: Show 3DS challenge
    
    Customer -> SDK: Complete 3DS
    SDK -> Router: POST /payments/{id}/confirm\n{authentication_result}
    Router -> Core: confirm_payment(payment_id)
    Core -> Connector: POST /v1/payment_intents/{id}/confirm
    Connector --> Core: 200 {status: succeeded}
    
else Payment Succeeded Immediately
    Connector --> Core: 200 OK\n{status: succeeded,\ncharge_id: ch_xxx}
    deactivate Connector
    
    Core -> DB: UPDATE payment_intent\nSET status = 'succeeded',\nconnector_payment_id = 'ch_xxx'
end

Core -> DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION

== Event Publishing ==

Core -> Events: XADD payment:events\n{event: payment.succeeded,\npayment_id, timestamp}
Events --> Core: stream_id

Core -> Cache: DEL payment:{id}:lock
Core -> Cache: SET payment:{id} (payment_data, EX 3600)

Core --> Router: PaymentResponse\n{payment_id, status: succeeded}
deactivate Core

Router --> SDK: 201 Created\n{payment_id, status, amount}
deactivate Router

SDK --> Customer: Show success message
deactivate SDK

== Async Processing ==

Events -> "Drainer": XREAD (blocking)\nSTREAM payment:events
activate "Drainer"

"Drainer" -> DB: INSERT payment_event_log
"Drainer" -> "Analytics": Aggregate metrics
"Drainer" -> "Webhook Service": Trigger merchant webhook

deactivate "Drainer"

== Scheduled Jobs ==

"Scheduler" -> DB: SELECT * FROM payments\nWHERE status = 'requires_capture'\nAND auto_capture_at < NOW()
activate "Scheduler"

"Scheduler" -> Router: POST /internal/payments/{id}/capture
"Scheduler" -> DB: UPDATE payment_intent\nSET status = 'processing'

deactivate "Scheduler"

note over Router, Connector
  **Error Handling:**
  - Network failures: Retry with exponential backoff
  - Idempotency: Use idempotency keys
  - Circuit breaker: Fail fast if connector down
  - Fallback: Route to alternate connector
end note

@enduml
